For anyone still coming to this thread, I adapted @participant2's [comment](https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/6322#issuecomment-1448141495), and it seems to work fairly well with a 1ms delay instead of 1ns. You'll have to slightly adjust the syntax.

```
use tauri::WindowEvent;
pub fn run() {
    tauri::Builder::default()
        .on_window_event(|_window, event| {
            if let WindowEvent::Resized(_) = event {
                std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(1));
            }
        })
        .plugin(tauri_plugin_shell::init())
        .run(tauri::generate_context!())
        .expect("error while running tauri application");
}
```
